[{"id": 1, "name": "St. Lamberti Church", "country": "Germany", "lat": 51.9629463, "lng": 7.6288524, "description": "A group of Anabaptists infamously took over the city of Munster in 1534-1535. While the city was besieged by the forces of the Catholic bishop they had expelled, the leaders inside multiplied atrocities. The city fell after a long siege, and the leaders were executed. Their corpses eventually rotted in the cages which still hang from this tower. Website: https://www.sanktlamberti.de/", "images": ["https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6NxN8Czy1pKOLLwoj2tC28sWcgoqIFdpmbnat5qlZefIkigPeeLk70V_xDRV0npaskecKNLZb0k_ZQUSDvLlrqz-8FwCuSl83kAxCceWeAr2lrQLGuszjGVQ9VRseCZD-LYlEh8dA529AxVYLumyb_g2Xnwp7VhCYV4ZOIOzntpd48ZttlY0e3PLaLqjPEUDeXybQ2aRc0I0Jv7X-rR28Et-DbL8wFjR_B0QQ1gr27Qf1o4aaN0efNWZQ?fife=w900", "https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4jeWBVX_gN3ZGgjEAvx2VTjBohvsMro21UWj-3KUyEoaGBNFucQMqsZm8jrLNUWNgU8jyiTtzsJ4Y7JoR7UbpmjCZx0OVrsJqZo5r41H8s-qhk1iChBSP-qhdomSiesGkt9CcjFrXflAdKQcku7Q4AhEEAojL_kN3VrXxC55SVYQk7q8SIoDz_Dv6WMLeQ5lNKt8CUiLuVj2Jz_WhhJ-iRuUMEj8vFRAkzrfrHwadyBX0V92H6_qMutDY?fife=w900"]}, {"id": 2, "name": "Strasbourg, France", "country": "France", "lat": 48.5801, "lng": 7.7393426, "description": "When the Anabaptist movement began in 1525, this city was Anabaptist friendly. It attracted a wide range of early Anabaptists, such as Michael Sattler, Pilgrim Marpeck, and Melchior Hoffman.", "images": ["https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4gR0WNwW84E4EOxfqto76cAwn9WLUc_68GVMjk9bMHgFn5ybczlnWH7m7qgl3FIqOzuJpGUr9O0DAM-7evmtZfxbyz9krWpoMrA9vBSD2rTaukaXsfEwixIwpJ_cE35Fd6__H3tUu183TENpevZp8UqQvpN-lUvz7y9VyrTl0Wvceg1Guf1Buuu79PBb2MEt2YpxLgyImh1TU9jrAw3t0OhD_1XS3U1ngjxkz0AZmuUMfpwzdIJ7JX-Hc?fife=w900", "https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6ZT_JcPSVZbZXjXL1XGVbuv78ErkPxi1-wdWh02D7ALLemVGurV2xDTpTomC6e39VXx1UML0mjmxKBtKOT6OMiFR7gqUUFWIILtSzwBmJjTPUGDIJKvvQUBn3nQ-fqqbWzK0